Apple today released <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> 27, the latest version of the macOS operating system that runs on the Mac. &zwnj;macOS Golden Gate&zwnj; is a free app that can be downloaded on all compatible Macs. The update requires a Mac with an Apple silicon chip, and it is not available on Intel Macs.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051479" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/macOS-27-next-to-MacBook-Pro-Running-macOS-27.jpg" alt="" width="2065" height="1162" /><br/>
Mac users can download the &zwnj;macOS Golden Gate&zwnj; update by using the Software Update section of System Settings. The update introduces <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI, a smarter chatbot version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; with a dedicated &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; app. It brings <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a> to the Mac for the first time, and tweaks the look of the Liquid Glass design update Apple introduced last year.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's release notes for &zwnj;macOS Golden Gate&zwnj; are below.<blockquote><strong>Experience the new Siri AI</strong><br/>
Introducing Siri AI, an entirely new version of Siri powered by Apple Intelligence that's more personal, more capable, and more conversational. It is integrated into Spotlight, so you can search for answers about almost any topic right from where you already search for things across your system. It can draw on personal context to find things across your messages, mail, photos, and more. And it can get things done across your apps, just by asking. Revisit and resume past conversations in the new dedicated Siri app, synced with iCloud across your Apple devices. Siri AI is rolling out to users, and you can get started by turning it on in Settings.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>Take action on what's onscreen</strong><br/>
With Visual Intelligence, you can select a window of your screen and Siri can answer questions or take action with what's onscreen, like adding events to your calendar. You can access Visual Intelligence with a dedicated keyboard shortcut — Command-Shift-Space.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>Powerful new ways to edit photos</strong><br/>
Use intelligent photo editing tools to reframe a photo after it's been taken with Spatial Reframing or expand your shot with the Extend tool. And enhancements to Clean Up let you remove distractions with better quality and more realistic infill, even when the scene is complex.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>New tools to browse in Safari</strong><br/>
Automatically group your tabs into topics, so related pages are easier to find. With Notify Me, Safari can monitor pages for changes like price drops or restocks and alert you when it's time to act. Describe an Extension lets you use natural language to create custom extensions, like adding a button to save your favorite recipes.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>Easily create Shortcuts using natural language</strong><br/>
With Describe a Shortcut, you can automate daily tasks with a simple description and all of the required steps are assembled on your behalf. For example, you can describe a shortcut to automatically text your partner when you're headed home from work with an estimated arrival time based on traffic.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>Even more refined design</strong><br/>
Updates to Liquid Glass improve readability, and a new slider lets you customize how it looks, from ultra-clear to fully tinted. Uniform toolbars, edge-to-edge sidebars, and more detailed app icons further elevate the design.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>New child safety features</strong><br/>
Powerful new parental controls help parents more easily manage what content their children can see, who they can communicate with, and when they have access to apps. Ask to Browse requires kids to request permission before visiting any new website in Safari. Communication Safety expands its protections to help keep conversations safe. Time Allowances gives parents more flexible ways to manage the time kids spend in apps across categories, and offers guidance based on expert research that's tailored to a child's age. Schedules help manage which apps kids have access to at different times of the day and across the week.<br/>
<br/>
<strong>A more responsive and delightful experience</strong><br/>
An expansive set of improvements make your Mac even faster, more reliable, and easier to use. Better search in Spotlight and Mail helps you find what you're looking for with greater ease. AirDrop Transfers and network file browsing happen faster. And many more improvements make your day-to-day use more enjoyable.</blockquote>For more on all of the new features in &zwnj;macOS Golden Gate&zwnj;, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">check out our dedicated roundup</a>.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a></div><div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forum: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/macos-golden-gate.253">macOS Golden Gate</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/apple-releases-macos-golden-gate/">macOS Golden Gate Now Available With Siri AI, Visual Intelligence and More</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/macos-golden-gate-now-available-with-siri-ai-visual-intelligence-and-more.2489282/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>